From 46c63d3541f0d3a112a76af6c93f947101b7f1dc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Paul Junod <donujp@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 10:15:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 06/12] clutter/color: Make display targets only through an
 explicit constructor

The blending state of any parametric state with a target luminance or
target primaries became a display target, the state highlight mapping
and gamut compression convert toward: a display reference luminance was
the only mark, and get_blending() set it from any target volume. So the
blending state of a client state with HDR10 mastering metadata would
have been a display target, mapping content toward the client's
mastering display.

Add clutter_color_state_params_new_display_target(), the only way to
make one, used only by the color device for an output's rendering color
state; it validates target primaries as a gamut target. A display target
is marked as such and part of the exact identity, equality and hash; the
blending states derived from it stay display targets. Any other state,
including one made with
clutter_color_state_params_new_with_target_volume(), is not, nor are its
blending states, which keep its target volume in the units of the state
they were derived from.

The tests make their sample targets the way the color device does, and
check that a target volume attached as content metadata, to a client
state or to the output state, never makes a display target for
highlight mapping or gamut compression, nor does it in a blending state.

Link: TBD-MR
